## How the vote works

Everyone gets the base pack (performance fixes, map, item search). The optional mods below are up for vote. Each one has a PC load rating so people on older laptops can see what they're signing up for.

Light barely noticeable Medium fine on 8 GB, more if you build big Heavy wants 16 GB and a decent GPU Suggested Alex's pick

**Rule of thumb**

- Pick one gun mod, not both. They do the same job and double the load.
- Create plus one electric tech mod is plenty for a first season. More can be added later.
- Anything marked Heavy needs a majority of the "yes" votes from people on weaker PCs, otherwise it stays out.

## Base pack (everyone gets these)

Not up for vote. These make the game run better and easier, and most of them are invisible in play.

## Factories & power

The industrial core. Create is the mechanical one (cogs, belts, steam), the others add electricity, cables and big machines.

## Mining & drilling

Ways to dig out ore without spending every evening with a pickaxe. Note that Create, Mekanism and Immersive Engineering each bring their own drill or miner too.

## Guns & combat

Two solid choices. Vote for the one you'd rather have, not both.

## Quality of life & world

Small additions that make a friends server nicer. All light.

## Server settings

Quick questions so the world is set up once, properly.

## Will my PC run it?

Rough guide for the base pack plus a normal set of picks. Allocated RAM is set automatically by the installer based on what your PC has.

**8 GB RAM, integrated graphics**Works with base pack + Create + one gun mod. Keep render distance at 8. Skip Heavy mods.

**16 GB RAM, any dedicated GPU**Comfortable with everything on this page at render distance 12.

**Older than 2016 or 4 GB RAM**Tell Alex before the vote closes. A cut-down pack or a fresh SSD/RAM upgrade might be needed.

**Mac or Linux**The one-click installer is Windows only. Alex will send a short manual guide.

